WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.285
The ablations show sparsification is essentially free.

00:00:04.365 --> 00:00:08.651
Pruning each sparse coding matrix to just
forty-eight non-zero elements,

00:00:08.731 --> 00:00:13.016
about three hundred thousand parameters,

00:00:13.096 --> 00:00:17.382
meets the storage budget while keeping ConvNet
accuracy at seventy-three point five percent,

00:00:17.462 --> 00:00:21.747
barely below the seventy-four percent of the full
fifteen-million-parameter model.

00:00:21.827 --> 00:00:26.113
Push k too low, down to twelve, and accuracy collapses,

00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:30.478
so a moderate value is best and even improves
cross-architecture generalization.

00:00:30.558 --> 00:00:34.844
On the network side, two recurrent blocks and three
heads work best.

00:00:34.924 --> 00:00:39.209
And qualitatively,

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:43.575
synthetic images before and after sparsification to
zero point three percent density look almost identical,

00:00:43.655 --> 00:00:47.940
confirming that the pruned features preserve the
global semantics.
